        "parms": "# kslider — a keyboard\nA kslider is a piano keyboard. Press a key and it sends a velocity, then the pitch; let go and it sends velocity 0, a release. Each of the 128 keys holds its own velocity, so several can be down at once. Its argument is the velocity a pitch on a cable plays at, 100 by default.\nMax's kslider is monophonic unless its mode is set to polyphonic. Here every key always holds its own velocity, and a <pitch> <velocity> list also sets the velocity for later pitches.",
